# Tiling Guidelines

---

## Tiling Calculations

Calculate tile size without margins. Required while processing layout when `paperType=tile` or `paperType=roll`.

### Reference

- [`docs/tiling-docs/TILING_CALCULATION_WORKFLOW.md`](../../docs/tiling-docs/TILING_CALCULATION_WORKFLOW.md)

### Inputs

| Source | Variables |
|--------|-----------|
| inputDOM | `inputDomWidth`, `inputDomHeight` |
| Settings | `tileWidth`, `tileHeight`, `marginLeft`, `marginRight`, `marginTop`, `marginBottom` |

### Formulas

```
trimTileWidth  = tileWidth - marginLeft - marginRight
trimTileHeight = tileHeight - marginTop - marginBottom

numTilesWidth  = floor(inputDomWidth / trimTileWidth) + ceil(remainder)
numTilesHeight = floor(inputDomHeight / trimTileHeight) + ceil(remainder)

pageWidth  = numTilesWidth  * trimTileWidth  + marginLeft + marginRight
pageHeight = numTilesHeight * trimTileHeight + marginTop  + marginBottom
```

### Key Constraints

- Applies when `media == paper` AND (`paperType == tile`)
- Tile IDs follow pattern: `Tile<row>_<col>`

---

## Tiling Reduction

Remove empty tiled rows from processed layout.

### Reference

- [`docs/tiling-docs/TILING_REDUCTION_WORKFLOW.txt`](../../docs/tiling-docs/TILING_REDUCTION_WORKFLOW.txt)

### When to Apply

After `process_layout()` completes, before displaying `layout_dom` in the right canvas.

### Required Functions

| Function | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `check_tile_single_piece_overlap(tileid, P)` | Returns true if piece P overlaps tile |
| `reduce_dom_height(dom, reduce_amt)` | Reduces contentRect, background, and SVG height |
| `check_tile_pieces_overlap(tileid)` | Returns true if any piece overlaps tile |
| `check_pieces_in_BottomTileRow(layout_dom)` | Checks if bottom row tiles have pieces |
| `clean_BottomTileRow(layout_dom, tile_list)` | Deletes empty bottom row, reduces height |
| `clean_BottomRollArea(layout_dom)` | Removes unused roll space (if > 20 units) |

### DOM Elements Modified

- `id=contentRect` — `height` attribute
- `id=background` — `height` attribute
- `<svg>` — `height` attribute
- `<tiledRects>` group — tile rectangles with `id="Tile<row>_<col>"`

### Reduction Logic

#### Tiled Paper
```
while !pieces_in_BottomTileRow:
    clean_BottomTileRow(layout_dom)
```

#### Roll Paper
```
space = contentRect.maxY - lowest_piece.maxY
if space > 20:
    reduce_dom_height(layout_dom, space)
```

### Key Constraints

- Only applies when `media == paper` AND (`paperType == tile` OR `paperType == roll`)
- Minimum space threshold for roll reduction: **20 units**